  "published": "2026-11-08T08:29:19.383Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "dotskit upgrade takes the parts one run after another and stops at conflicts; --continue resumes.\n\n- dotskit upgrade walks every part of the upgrade in one run, committing each, and stops at a part in conflict: resolve it the way any merge is resolved, then dotskit upgrade --continue finishes; the run names what is left.\n- When a build fails mid-upgrade the message no longer promises a commit that did not happen: it names what is left and the remedy - fix the build and continue with dotskit upgrade --continue.\n- DOTSKIT_TEMPLATE_PACKAGES names a folder of nupkg files the tool installs the template from instead of nuget.org - for CI and machines without the registry; the default stays nuget.org.\n\nHow to update a solution generated from an earlier version: https://github.com/sawking-tech/DotNetSolutionKit/blob/v2.9.1/docs/getting-started/upgrading.md",
